## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical skills designing a rigorous evaluation framework for a multilingual policy assistant that must ensure every factual claim maps to a live source while detecting cross-source conflicts and tracking policy drift over time.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual policy alignment and factual consistency
- Versioned source management and drift detection
- Cross-source hallucination detection for conflicting information
- Automated evaluation with comprehensive metrics and tooling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal verification framework: map claims to source citations
function verifyClaim(claim, sources) {
  const citation = findSourceCitation(claim, sources);
  return {
    claim,
    source: citation.url,
    timestamp: citation.version,
    isValid: validateClaim(claim, citation)
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of attention scaling, memory constraints, and practical trade-offs in production-grade transformers.

## Key Concepts
- Block-local attention and memory scaling
- Attention masking within a window
- Q/K/V reshaping for block processing
- Trade-offs: accuracy vs latency vs memory

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: local attention in blocks
function localAttention(Q, K, V, block=256, window=128){
  // Q,K,V: [B, T, D]
  const B = Q.length, T = Q[0].length, D = Q[0][0].length;
  let O = Array.from({length:B}, () => Array.from({length:T}, () => new Array(D).fill(0)));
  for (let b=0; b<B; b++){
    for (let s=0; s<T; s+=block){
      const end = Math.min(T, s+block);
      for (let t=s; t<end; t++){
        const wStart = Math.max(0, t-window);
        const wEnd = Math.min(T, t+window+1);
        // compute attention over [wStart, wEnd)
        // A = softmax((Q[t]·K[w].T)/sqrt(D))
        // O[b][t] = sum_{w=wStart}^{wEnd-1} A[w]·V[w]
      }
    }
  }
  return O;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How does changing window size affect long-range dependency capture and memory?
- What metrics would you monitor to detect degradation when switching from global to local attention?
